const e="kerala-school-sasthrolsavam-maths-fair",c=2025,t="Read in full from the Kerala School Sasthrolsavam Manual 2025 (Malayalam; 250 PDF pages): Chapters 1-5 (common rules, levels, committees, appeals, championship), Chapter 7 (Mathematics Fair) and the entry forms and annexures. The manual is in a legacy font, so every page was read from its image; page numbers in Source are the printed numbers. The manual prints no dates for the 2025 festival, no venue or address, no phone numbers or e-mail, no website for the online entry, no fixed last date to register, and no cash amount for prizes. These are not captured. The only dated item is the order of 12 September 2025 (a news Variable). Amounts printed (appeal fees, registration fee at the sub-district fair, fee for a new certificate) are Variables. The manual prints no score table for Maths Quiz and Talent Search Examination. The manual's Magazine score list on p.80 and the score table on p.77 word the last two marks differently; the table is used and the other wording is in Notes. The Teaching Aid competition for maths teachers is not in the template (teachers only) and is named in one item under Other Parts of the Manual with its printed rules and marks. The Kerala School Skill Festival and the other fairs of the manual are named in one line under Other Parts of the Manual.",a=JSON.parse('{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"Kerala School Sasthrolsavam, Mathematics Fair. Read these rules before you register.","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"The Mathematics Fair is held for LP, UP, HS and HSS/VHSS children at the school, sub-district, revenue district and state levels. The head master or principal registers the entries online.","Notes":["A child can take part in only one item of one fair, and in the quiz of one field.","A school sends to the next level only the first place winners with an A grade at the school fair.","Make the entries with the photo of every child.","On-the-spot items take 3 hours. Bring all the materials you need. Do not bring calculators, mobile phones, notes or ready cut materials.","A complaint about a result must be given within one hour after the result is announced."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["The Kerala School Sasthrolsavam is the Science, Mathematics, Social Science, Work Experience and IT fair of the children in LP, UP, HS, Higher Secondary and Vocational Higher Secondary classes of the Government, Aided and Unaided (recognised) schools of Kerala under the General Education Department.","All earlier Science, Maths, Social Science, Work Experience and IT fair manuals and amendments are cancelled by this manual.","The competitions are held from school level to state level on the dates in the education calendar that the department publishes each year, or on the dates the Director of General Education gives.","The fair of each school is held by the clubs of the school. The fairs of the sub-district and revenue district are held by the club associations or councils of that level. The state fair is held by the department and the state club associations or councils.","The Director of General Education gives the directions needed to run the Kerala School Sasthrolsavam.","The fairs are held on the subject that is told from time to time under the rules and directions of the General Education Department.","Aim: to grow scientific, mathematical, social science, work experience and IT interest and research interest in the children, and to grow what they learn in a way that helps the society they live in.","Aim: to train the children to use well in daily life the knowledge they gain from science and technology, mathematics, social science, work experience and IT.","Aim: to help the children know the link between people and their surroundings and understand the method of gaining this knowledge.","Aim: to grow the inquiry mind and the research mind along with the gain of knowledge.","Aim: to find and nurture the natural abilities of the children.","Aim: to understand current events against the background of past and lasting history, and to keep them for the future generation in a useful way.","Aim: to introduce the importance and use of free software.","Aim: to give chances to know new technical fields in IT and use them, to do creative work with digital media, and to practise a computer language.","Aim: to make the children able to win their own scientific and technical achievements in the future, and to gain practical skill in science, maths, social science, work experience and IT.","The Mathematics Fair has on-the-spot construction competitions to find and encourage the real abilities of children. The Group Project, the Single Project and the Magazine are not on-the-spot competitions.","In an on-the-spot construction competition each item takes 3 hours.","No object made outside can be used in an on-the-spot competition. A calculator, a digital diary, a PC, photos, a mobile phone, notes, and objects that are cut or marked cannot be brought into the competition hall.","All competitors bring all the materials needed for the competition.","Paper, charts, card boards and wooden boards used for making must not be cut to a usable size and brought. They must be used as they are.","A short write up of the idea that is presented (at most 3 pages) is given to the invigilator.","A child can be given 5 to 8 minutes for the presentation.","The exhibition must be held at all levels.","Children must use materials that are friendly to nature (eco friendly) to make exhibits. Thermocol and PC sheet are not used at all.","A chart can be made on the content of the curriculum of that level. If the idea is not complete in one chart, a second and a third chart can be used. At most three charts can be made on one idea, written on one side only. Each chart is 72 cm x 56 cm. Charts are not stuck together. The matter is written and drawn in a suitable size and form on each chart."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Eligibility","Items":["Children of the Government, Aided and Unaided (recognised) schools under the General Education Department of Kerala can take part.","The competition is held in four categories by class. Category I is class 1 to 4 (LP). Category II is class 5 to 7 (UP). Category III is class 8 to 10 (HS). Category IV is class 11 and 12 (HSS and VHSS).","Category I and II competitions end at the sub-district level. Category III and IV competitions go up to the state level.","A school fair is open to every child of the school. Every child gets the chance to take part by category.","Only a competitor who got first place with an A grade in the item at the school fair can take part in the sub-district competition.","In Category III and IV, only a competitor who got the first or second place with an A grade at the sub-district level can take part in the revenue district competition, and only a competitor who got the first or second place with an A grade at the revenue district level can take part in the state competition.","A child can take part in only one item of one of the five fairs (Science, Maths, Social Science, Work Experience, IT). In addition, the child can take part in the quiz competition of any one field.","A competitor with marks below 60 percent in an item gets no grade. If only one child takes part in an item, the child goes to the sub-district fair only if the performance is good enough for a grade.","If nobody gets first place with an A grade in an item at the school fair, no competitor is sent from the school to the sub-district fair for that item.","If two competitors get equal marks for the first or the second place in an item at the school fair, the competitor for the upper level is chosen by the total marks of the evaluation plus the marks for evaluation criterion (A).","A school can take part at the sub-district level only if it is affiliated to the science, maths, social science, work experience and IT club association or council of that sub-district.","A sub-district can take part at the revenue district level only if it is affiliated to the club association or council of that revenue district.","All district level clubs of a revenue district must be affiliated to the state club association or council before the revenue district takes part in the state fair.","At the sub-district fair, the competitor brings the school level certificate that the head master or principal of the school has attested.","At the revenue district fair, the competitor brings the certificate of recognition from the head master or principal of the school, attested by the sub-district education officer.","At the state fair, the competitor brings the certificate of recognition from the head master or principal of the school, attested by the Deputy Director of Education.","Only two competitors from a sub-district or a revenue district can take part in an item at the next higher level, on merit.","Before a court or an appeal authority gives an order on a request of a competitor, it must be made sure that only two competitors take part at the higher level and that the third competitor does not come. If a court or an appeal authority allows a third competitor by a clear order, the performance of the competitors who already qualified is evaluated again, one is left out, and only two from one place take part in an item at the higher level (High Court judgment W.A. No. 1178/2017 dated 22.6.2017).","Each school at the sub-district fair brings an escorting teacher. If girls take part, a woman teacher must go with the team as an escorting teacher. The teachers carry the full responsibility for the children.","Maths LP is for children of classes 1 to 4, Maths UP for classes 5 to 7, Maths HS for classes 8 to 10 and Maths HSS/VHSS for classes 11 and 12.","A student can take part in only one item of the Mathematics Fair.","In the Magazine competition the children do not take part. The members of the maths club of the school prepare the magazine.","The Group Project is entered by 2 children. The part of each child must be clear.","The Madhava Paper Presentation is for the UP section only. The Bhaskaracharya Seminar is for the HS section only. The Srinivasa Ramanujan Paper Presentation is for the HSS/VHSS section only.","The Talent Search Examination is for the UP, HS and HSS/VHSS sections.","The Teaching Aid competition is only for teachers who teach the maths subject."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Register","Items":["All competitions from the sub-district level to the state level, including the club level competitions, are held on the online system. The head master or principal makes the online entry of the children with great care.","The photo of every child must be uploaded at the time of registration.","The full responsibility for the online entries is with the head master or principal.","After the sub-district competitions, the list of the competitors chosen for the revenue district competitions is registered online.","The state fair registration committee registers the teams that come from the different districts, gives the registration cards and passes their details to the accommodation committee. It also gives the food coupons to the committees and the team managers.","At the state fair, each competitor gives a short description of the exhibit, with photos, at the time of the competition.","Competitors must come to the place of the competition on the time fixed. A competitor who does not come on time can be made ineligible.","The rules and conditions of each competition item are announced on the stage before the competition starts.","The programme committee gives the code numbers for the competitors from the office of the Director of General Education.","The entry forms of the manual give the details of the school, the competitors and the escorting teachers. The sub-district entry form carries the school name and school (Sampoorna) code, the type of school (Government, Aided or Unaided), the number of boys, girls and others, and the name, designation, phone number and signature of the escorting teacher, with the signature of the head of the institution. The head of the school also signs a declaration that the details agree with the school records and with the manual.","The revenue district and state entry forms carry the name of the sub-district or revenue district, the number of boys and girls, the name of each item, the name of each child in capital letters, the name of the school, the class, the sex and remarks. The state fair form also names the team manager and the escorting teachers with their addresses and carries the signature and seal of the Deputy Director of Education."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Fees and Payment","Items":["A registration fee of {{SubDistrictRegistrationFee}} can be collected at the sub-district fair.","The funds for the sub-district fair come from the scheme fund, the special fee fund, public donations, the funds of the science, maths, social science, work experience and IT clubs, and PTA donations.","The funds are spent as per the budget that the organising committee approves. The accounts of the fair are presented to the concerned committee and passed within one month after the fair.","The income and expenses of the funds that the scheme gives are approved by the organising committee within one month after the fair, and then given to the treasury of the education officer.","At state level, the Finance Committee gives the budget of all committees to the organising committee for approval, allows unexpected expenses in advance (to be approved later), and helps the General Convener to prepare the accounts for audit. The audited accounts are approved by the organising committee within one month after the fair.","The committees can take gifts and donations of articles as the organising committee approves. A special register is kept for this and the General Convener signs it.","An appeal costs a fee that depends on the level. There is no appeal fee at the school level (see Complaints and Appeals).","The fee for a new certificate is given under Prizes and Certificates."]},{"Key":"levels","Title":"Levels and Qualification","Items":["The Sasthrolsavam has four levels: school, sub-district, revenue district and state.","School level: the fair is held in one day under the science, maths, social science, work experience and IT clubs of the school. Every child of the school gets the chance to take part by category.","The school fair committee has the ward member as chairman, the PTA president or the SMC chairman as vice chairman, the principal or the first teacher as General Convener, the first teacher or the senior assistant as joint General Convener, the club coordinators as joint convenors, and all teachers, PTA and SMC members, mother PTA members and the school leader as members. Sub-committees can be formed.","Sub-district level (LP, UP, HS, HSS and VHSS): the fair is held in two days. The sub-district education officer, the RDD or AD of Higher Secondary and Vocational Higher Secondary, and the club secretaries choose a suitable school together. The sub-district clubs hold the fair. There are separate competitions for LP, UP, HS and HSS/VHSS, and HSS and VHSS are one unit.","Sub-district winners get certificates and encouragement awards.","The sub-district organising committee has the MPs, MLAs, and the presidents of district, block and grama panchayats, the mayor and the municipal chairmen as patrons; the mayor, municipal chairman or grama panchayat president as chairman; the principal or head master of the venue school as General Convener; the club secretaries as convenors; and the sub-district education officer as treasurer.","Revenue district level (HS, HSS and VHSS): the committees are formed by the Deputy Directors of Education. The fair is held in two days. The Deputy Director of Education, the RDD, the AD and the club secretaries, with the Kite district coordinator, choose suitable schools together. All sub-districts of the revenue district must take part.","At the revenue district fair, HS and HSS/VHSS are evaluated separately. The evaluation records are kept for one year in the office of the Deputy Director of Education. Winners get certificates and encouragement awards.","The revenue district organising committee has the ministers, MPs, MLAs, district panchayat president, mayor, municipal chairmen, District Collector and District Police Chief as patrons; the local MLA as chairman; the Deputy Director of Education as General Convener; and the District Educational Officer of the education district as treasurer.","State level (HS, HSS and VHSS): the fair is held in three days under the General Education Department and the state science, maths, social science, work experience and IT association or council. The Director of General Education decides the place of the fair. All revenue districts of the state must take part.","At the state fair the first three places in each item get certificates, cash awards and honours.","The state organising committee has the Governor, the Chief Minister, the Leader of the Opposition, the Minister of General Education and the ministers of the host district as chief patrons. The Director of General Education is the General Coordinator and the Additional Director of General Education (Academic) is the General Convener.","The state organising (co-ordination) committee is fully responsible for the state fair. It prepares the budget, approves the sums for the sub-committees, approves the income and expense plan of the finance committee, and joins all sub-committees to work together.","The state sub-committees are the Programme, Reception, Exhibition and Cultural, Food, Pandal and Stage, Finance, Publicity, Law and Order, Welfare, Registration, Accommodation, Transport, Trophy, Light and Sound, Souvenir and Green Protocol committees.","In the Mathematics Fair, the Magazine of the LP section goes up to the sub-district level, the Magazine of the UP section goes up to the revenue district level, and the Magazine of the HS and HSS/VHSS sections goes up to the state level."]},{"Key":"teams","Title":"Teams, Team Managers and Escorting Teachers","Items":["Each school at the sub-district fair brings an escorting teacher with its team. If girls take part, a woman teacher must go with the team as an escorting teacher.","At the revenue district fair, the team manager of each sub-district team is the sub-district education officer, and the joint team manager is the sub-district secretary of the club association.","At the state fair, each revenue district team has a team manager. Each section has escorting teachers. The secretaries of the district associations are joint team managers. Women teachers go with the girls."]},{"Key":"points","Title":"Points and Grading","Items":["A competitor who gets 60 percent marks or more in an item gets a grade. Grade A is 80 percent or more and gives 5 points. Grade B is 70 percent to 79 percent and gives 3 points. Grade C is 60 percent to 69 percent and gives 1 point.","Items that get less than 60 percent marks are not graded.","Place points: the first place gets 5 points, the second place gets 3 points and the third place gets 1 point.","For the overall championship, the total of the grade points and the place points is counted. If the totals are equal, the number of first places is counted.","Sub-district level: the best school in each of LP, UP, HS and HSS/VHSS is found from the total points of all the fairs. The schools with the best show in each of the Science, Maths, Social Science, Work Experience and IT fairs are also found.","Revenue district level: the best sub-districts and the best schools are found. The championship of HS and of HSS/VHSS is decided from the total points of the five fairs. The schools and sub-districts with the best show in each fair are also found.","State level: the best districts, sub-districts and schools are found. The championship of HS and of HSS/VHSS is decided from the total points of the five fairs. The districts and schools with the best show in each fair are also found.","Only the competition items that are part of a fair count for the championship of that fair.","In the Mathematics Fair, the points of the Bhaskaracharya Seminar and the Srinivasa Ramanujan Paper Presentation are not counted for the championship. The result of the Magazine is not counted for the championship of the fair either.","The grade of the Maths Quiz is decided on the points of the first place winner in the quiz."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Prizes and Certificates","Items":["Competitors who get a grade receive certificates from the school level.","Winners at the sub-district and revenue district fairs get certificates and encouragement awards.","At the state fair, the first three places in each item get certificates, cash awards and honours.","At the closing ceremony of the state fair, the overall championships are given with their certificates and special honours.","The trophy committee collects the trophies of the last year, repairs and polishes them, and prepares the trophies and certificates from the list that the programme committee gives every day. They are given on the same days. Trophies and certificates not given are counted, entered in the trophy register and given to the concerned Deputy Director of Education.","The team manager or the escorting teacher signs the trophy register as clear proof of receiving the trophies.","When the competitions are over, the trophy register is completed and handed to the concerned education officer. At the state level it is handed to the PRO.","Everrolling trophies and shields last for ten years. After that, if the donors do not give new ones, the Director of General Education takes them back.","If a certificate given by the Director of General Education is lost or has errors, the head master or principal sends an application with a demand draft of {{CertificateReplacementFee}} in the name of the Director of General Education to get a new certificate."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Conduct and Safety","Items":["The whole Kerala School Sasthrolsavam must be held strictly under the Green Protocol.","A student, teacher or other person who tries to spoil the Sasthrolsavam by shameless, undisciplined or provoking behaviour gets a proper punishment, including being made ineligible. Action by the department can also be taken.","Only items that keep the safety of the children can be held, from school level to state level. The organisers must take special care to arrange all safety measures.","The Law and Order Committee keeps discipline and order at the venue of the fair, with the help of police officers, SPC, NCC, scouts, guides, other helpful organisations and leading citizens. Police service must be there until the fair ends.","Light is arranged at all places at all times. Plug points are arranged on the stages and stalls (at least 5 power plugs in each room of the exhibition stalls), with a generator and a sound system. The certificates for electrical safety are given to the General Convener 2 days before the fair starts.","The Public Works Department gives the fitness certificate of the stages, and it goes to the General Convener 2 days before the fair starts. The fire force is arranged and a pandal is given for it.","The Welfare Committee looks after the welfare and health of the participants and officials. Medical help and first aid are available at all times with the Public Health Department. Cleaning of the place of stay, the competition places, the food halls and the surroundings is arranged with the local self government department. Drinking water must be there everywhere.","The Green Protocol Committee has the Suchitwa Mission district coordinator as its chairman, gives directions to keep the stages and the surroundings clean and green, gives awareness of the Green Protocol to the competitors and the viewers, and gives guidelines to avoid plastic."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Judges and Judging","Items":["Judges are fair, well known and capable persons. When judges are chosen, their bio data and declaration are taken in writing, as in the annexure. At every level at least three judges must be there to judge.","A person cannot be a judge in the science fairs and the related competitions for more than two years. A sub-district judge cannot be a judge at the revenue district fair of the same revenue district. A district level judge cannot be a judge at the state Sasthrolsavam or its related competitions in the same year.","Every year the Director of General Education chooses the state and district judges from the nominations of persons from the Government institutions of the state, the Government recognised education institutions, experts in the subjects and persons in higher education, after a careful check. The Deputy Directors of Education are responsible for choosing the sub-district judges by the same standard.","The programme committee gives the judges the score sheets and the remark sheets in time, and collects and keeps their bio data and declaration.","The score sheet with the evaluation indicators gets the approval of the General Convener.","There must be no cutting or correction on a score sheet. If a correction cannot be avoided, the person who evaluated must sign it fully at the place.","A judge gives an evaluation note, with an opinion, for each child along with the score sheet.","After each competition the score sheet, the remark sheet, the tabulation sheet and the report of the stage manager are collected. The points are written on the score board in time.","The mark lists of the competitions and the tabulation sheets of the results are sealed and kept for one year in the office of the sub-district education officer (or the Deputy Director of Education at revenue district level). They are produced when the appeal committee or higher officers ask for them.","The programme committee prepares the results and uploads them, and gives the results to the trophy committee and the publicity committee in time. It prepares, with the Kite, the list of winners for the higher level competitions and gives it to the upper levels.","All item competitions are recorded on video, and a CD is prepared to help the appeal committee study the complaints. For on-the-spot competitions the video is recorded when the products are finished. The programme committee is responsible for this."]},{"Key":"complaints","Title":"Complaints and Appeals","Items":["An appeal committee must be formed at every level to give judgment on complaints about the results of the Science, Maths, Social Science, Work Experience and IT fairs.","The appeal committees consider appeals on the basis of the judgments of the Honourable High Court on this matter and the rules in the manual. The decision of the appeal committee is final.","A complaint must be given to the appeal committee within one hour after the result is announced. An appeal given after one hour is not accepted for any reason.","The appeal committee studies the complaints clearly, gives its decision and issues the order of action on the appeal in the format of the annexure.","There is no appeal fee at the school level. The appeal fee is {{AppealFeeSubDistrict}} at the sub-district level, {{AppealFeeRevenueDistrict}} at the revenue district level, {{AppealFeeState}} at the state level and {{AppealFeeHigher}} for a higher appeal.","If the decision is in favour of the appeal, the appeal fee is given back. If not, the amount is added to the fund of the organising committee.","The school level appeal committee has the principal or head master and the coordinators of the school science, maths, social science, work experience and IT clubs (one representative of each). Only the competitor who got first place with an A grade at the school level can go to the sub-district fair. The appeal committee confirms this at the time of the appeal check.","The sub-district appeal committee has the District Education Officer as chairman, the sub-district education officer as vice chairman, one representative each of the RDD and the AD, the General Convener and one expert in the subject. Complaints go through the escorting teacher, in the fixed form, with the fixed fee, within one hour after the result is announced. Only complaints given through the escorting teacher are considered.","The revenue district appeal committee has the Deputy Director of Education as chairman, the RDD or AD as vice chairman, the District Education Officer, the Kite district coordinator and an expert or the regional foreman in the subject. Complaints go through the team manager, in the fixed form, with the fixed fee. Only complaints given through the team manager are considered.","The state appeal committee has the Director of General Education as chairman, the Additional Director (Academic) as vice chairman, the Director of Higher Secondary Education, the Director of Vocational Higher Secondary Education, the vice chairman and executive director of Kite, and an expert in the subject. Complaints go through the revenue district team manager or joint team manager, in the fixed form with the fixed fee. Only complaints given through the team manager are considered.","A competitor who goes to a higher level because of a court order or an order of an appeal authority is counted as a participant.","The members of the appeal committee and the judges give a declaration in the format of the annexure."]},{"Key":"other","Title":"Other Parts of the Manual","Items":["This page covers the Mathematics Fair only. The Sasthrolsavam also has the Science Fair, Social Science Fair, Work Experience Fair, IT Fair. Each has its own page.","The manual also holds the Kerala School Skill Festival for the students of the Vocational Higher Secondary courses, with its own manual part. It is held along with the Sasthrolsavam and is not covered here.","The manual has annexures: the entry forms for each fair and level, the evaluation sheets, a regional list of VHS schools, the format of the identity card for a child, the declaration for judges and appeal committee members, the application form for an appeal and the format of the appeal order.","The Programme Committee of the state fair keeps the competitor lists, score sheets, time sheets, tabulation sheets and score boards, gives the code numbers and a leaflet of instructions, and appoints and names teachers for the smooth running of the competitions. It also gives notices on the stages and keeps the time of every competition as planned. It sees to the internet and wi-fi, computers and equipment at each place, and the printing of certificates and the uploading of results.","The Reception Committee makes the list of persons to be invited to the opening and the closing, invites the guests, prints and gives invitations with the approval of the protocol officer, and receives the guests, the judges and the teams that come from the districts.","The Exhibition and Cultural Committee makes all the facilities for the exhibition (with the evaluation committee) at the venue school, keeps the exhibits from the districts safe, arranges facilities for judges to evaluate at the stalls, and lets the students and the public visit all stalls. It also gives code numbers and stall numbers for each district and arranges cultural programmes after the exhibition time.","The Food Committee gives food to the students, teachers, guests, judges, officials, organising committee members, volunteers and media persons. On the evaluation day food is given at the stalls. The special food items needed by the competitors of the on-the-spot competitions must be given at the competition place.","The Pandal and Stage Committee builds the pandals for the on-the-spot competitions and the exhibition stalls, with separate stalls for each section of each district, and separate stalls for the Primary, HS, HSS and VHSS teaching aids and teacher projects, for the Work Experience on-the-spot competitions and for the exhibition. It also builds the pandals for the opening and the closing, with toilets and urinals, chairs and furniture.","The Publicity Committee gives publicity for all the matters of the Sasthrolsavam in audio, visual and print media, banners and arches, and makes sure the competition results from the Programme Committee reach the news media in time.","The Accommodation Committee decides the place of stay for the teams that have completed registration, and arranges water, light, bathrooms and toilets. The stay of the judges, the officials and the committee convenors at the state fair is kept with the Public Relations Officer of the Directorate of General Education.","The Transport Committee arranges vehicles for the teams and guests that come to the fair, and asks the railway, the State Transport, the private bus owners and the school buses for special services to the venue and back.","The Souvenir Committee prepares and publishes the Sasthrolsavam Souvenir (Sasthrolsava Rekha). It collects articles, photos and advertisements with the approval of the General Convener, takes advertisement amounts at the tariff rate, bears the cost of the publication, gives the Souvenir with details and pictures to the General Convener within one month after the fair, and sends copies to the District Education Offices and the Higher Secondary and Vocational Higher Secondary Directorates.","The Teaching Aid competition for maths teachers (Primary, HS and HSS/VHSS sections) is in this chapter of the manual but is not a student competition. The teacher shows ideas of the lessons with charts, models and other aids. Winners (first and second place) at the sub-district fair take part at the revenue district fair, and winners (first and second place) at the revenue district fair take part at the state fair. At the state level the first, second and third place winners get a certificate and a cash award. The score table is Knowledge of content and mathematical value 30, Relationship with the curriculum 20, Mode of presentation and write up 25, Utility and classroom impact 15, Exhibition 10."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"Kerala School Sasthrolsavam Manual 2025 (PDF)","Url":"https://mela.kite.kerala.gov.in/2026/entry_forms/sasthrolsavam_manual_2025.pdf"},{"Title":"Kerala School Sasthrolsavam Item List 2026 (KITE)","Url":"https://mela.kite.kerala.gov.in/2026/index.php/Home/item_list"}]}'),i=[{ParticipantType:"Individual",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.7 A, p.67",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Almost every item of the Mathematics Fair is for one child. One child takes part in each item.","A child takes part in only one item of the fair."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Almost every item of the Mathematics Fair is for one child. One child takes part in each item.
- A child takes part in only one item of the fair.`},{ParticipantType:"Team",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.7 A c) 11, p.68 and D 9, p.74",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["The Group Project is the only team item. Two children take part, and the part of each child must be clear."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- The Group Project is the only team item. Two children take part, and the part of each child must be clear.`}],n=[{AgeGroup:"Maths LP",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.7 A a), p.67",Sections:{About:["The LP section is for children of classes 1 to 4."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["The items are Number Chart, Geometrical Chart, Still Model, Puzzle, Maths Magazine (the children do not take part in it) and Maths Quiz.","Every competition of this section ends at the sub-district level."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- The LP section is for children of classes 1 to 4.

## Rules
- The items are Number Chart, Geometrical Chart, Still Model, Puzzle, Maths Magazine (the children do not take part in it) and Maths Quiz.
- Every competition of this section ends at the sub-district level.`},{AgeGroup:"Maths UP",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.7 A b), p.67",Sections:{About:["The UP section is for children of classes 5 to 7."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["The items are Number Chart, Geometrical Chart, Still Model, Puzzle, Game, Maths Magazine (the children do not take part in it) and Maths Quiz. The Madhava Paper Presentation and the Talent Search Examination are also held for this section.","Every competition of this section ends at the sub-district level, except the Magazine, which goes up to the revenue district level."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- The UP section is for children of classes 5 to 7.

## Rules
- The items are Number Chart, Geometrical Chart, Still Model, Puzzle, Game, Maths Magazine (the children do not take part in it) and Maths Quiz. The Madhava Paper Presentation and the Talent Search Examination are also held for this section.
- Every competition of this section ends at the sub-district level, except the Magazine, which goes up to the revenue district level.`},{AgeGroup:"Maths HS",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.7 A c), pp.67-68",Sections:{About:["The HS section is for children of classes 8 to 10."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["The items are Number Chart, Geometrical Chart, Other Chart, Still Model, Working Model, Pure Construction, Construction Using Geogebra Software, Puzzle, Game, Single Project, Group Project (2 children), Maths Magazine (the children do not take part in it) and Maths Quiz. The Bhaskaracharya Seminar and the Talent Search Examination are also held for this section."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- The HS section is for children of classes 8 to 10.

## Rules
- The items are Number Chart, Geometrical Chart, Other Chart, Still Model, Working Model, Pure Construction, Construction Using Geogebra Software, Puzzle, Game, Single Project, Group Project (2 children), Maths Magazine (the children do not take part in it) and Maths Quiz. The Bhaskaracharya Seminar and the Talent Search Examination are also held for this section.`},{AgeGroup:"Maths HSS/VHSS",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.7 A c), pp.67-68",Sections:{About:["The HSS/VHSS section is for children of classes 11 and 12."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["The items are Number Chart, Geometrical Chart, Other Chart, Still Model, Working Model, Pure Construction, Construction Using Geogebra Software, Puzzle, Game, Single Project, Group Project (2 children), Maths Magazine (the children do not take part in it) and Maths Quiz. The Srinivasa Ramanujan Paper Presentation and the Talent Search Examination are also held for this section."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- The HSS/VHSS section is for children of classes 11 and 12.

## Rules
- The items are Number Chart, Geometrical Chart, Other Chart, Still Model, Working Model, Pure Construction, Construction Using Geogebra Software, Puzzle, Game, Single Project, Group Project (2 children), Maths Magazine (the children do not take part in it) and Maths Quiz. The Srinivasa Ramanujan Paper Presentation and the Talent Search Examination are also held for this section.`}],o=JSON.parse('[{"Title":"Number Chart","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.7 D (Chart section) 1, p.70 and E 1, p.74","Sections":{"About":["A chart that shows number patterns, number series, different kinds of numbers and the special features of numbers.","This item is held for LP, UP, HS and HSS/VHSS."],"TimeAndFormat":["This is an on-the-spot competition of 3 hours."],"Rules":["Each chart is 72 cm x 56 cm. At most 3 charts, written on one side only, can be used for one idea.","The chart can be drawn on with pencil, and the matter is written and drawn in a suitable size and form."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Knowledge of content and mathematical value: 30 marks.","Relationship with the curriculum: 20 marks.","Mode of presentation and write up: 25 marks.","Beauty and perfection: 15 marks.","Exhibition: 10 marks.","The total is 100 marks."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A chart that shows number patterns, number series, different kinds of numbers and the special features of numbers.\\n- This item is held for LP, UP, HS and HSS/VHSS.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- This is an on-the-spot competition of 3 hours.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each chart is 72 cm x 56 cm. At most 3 charts, written on one side only, can be used for one idea.\\n- The chart can be drawn on with pencil, and the matter is written and drawn in a suitable size and form.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Knowledge of content and mathematical value: 30 marks.\\n- Relationship with the curriculum: 20 marks.\\n- Mode of presentation and write up: 25 marks.\\n- Beauty and perfection: 15 marks.\\n- Exhibition: 10 marks.\\n- The total is 100 marks."},{"Title":"Geometrical Chart","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.7 D (Chart section) 2, pp.70-71 and E 2, p.75","Sections":{"About":["Charts that show the beauty of geometry by joining different geometric shapes. They can be made with geometric patterns, linear tessellation, spiralling and similar techniques.","This item is held for LP, UP, HS and HSS/VHSS."],"TimeAndFormat":["This is an on-the-spot competition of 3 hours."],"Rules":["Weight is given to the effective use of the chart and its style.","Colour can be applied to the chart.","Each chart is 72 cm x 56 cm. At most 3 charts, written on one side only, can be used for one idea."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Knowledge of content and mathematical value: 30 marks.","Relationship with the curriculum: 20 marks.","Mode of presentation and write up: 25 marks.","Beauty and perfection: 15 marks.","Exhibition: 10 marks.","The total is 100 marks."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Charts that show the beauty of geometry by joining different geometric shapes. They can be made with geometric patterns, linear tessellation, spiralling and similar techniques.\\n- This item is held for LP, UP, HS and HSS/VHSS.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- This is an on-the-spot competition of 3 hours.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Weight is given to the effective use of the chart and its style.\\n- Colour can be applied to the chart.\\n- Each chart is 72 cm x 56 cm. At most 3 charts, written on one side only, can be used for one idea.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Knowledge of content and mathematical value: 30 marks.\\n- Relationship with the curriculum: 20 marks.\\n- Mode of presentation and write up: 25 marks.\\n- Beauty and perfection: 15 marks.\\n- Exhibition: 10 marks.\\n- The total is 100 marks."},{"Title":"Other Chart","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.7 D (Chart section) 3, p.71 and E 3, p.75","Sections":{"About":["Charts that cannot be put in a number chart or a geometrical chart. They can hold the history of mathematics, any idea of mathematics, the history and events of mathematicians, graphs and writings about mathematics.","This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS."],"TimeAndFormat":["This is an on-the-spot competition of 3 hours."],"Rules":["The matter must give priority to ideas of mathematics and not be only a study of history.","Pictures of mathematicians are not to be put in.","Each chart is 72 cm x 56 cm. At most 3 charts, written on one side only, can be used for one idea."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Knowledge of content and mathematical value: 30 marks.","Relationship with the curriculum: 20 marks.","Mode of presentation and write up: 25 marks.","Beauty and perfection: 15 marks.","Exhibition: 10 marks.","The total is 100 marks."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Charts that cannot be put in a number chart or a geometrical chart. They can hold the history of mathematics, any idea of mathematics, the history and events of mathematicians, graphs and writings about mathematics.\\n- This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- This is an on-the-spot competition of 3 hours.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The matter must give priority to ideas of mathematics and not be only a study of history.\\n- Pictures of mathematicians are not to be put in.\\n- Each chart is 72 cm x 56 cm. At most 3 charts, written on one side only, can be used for one idea.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Knowledge of content and mathematical value: 30 marks.\\n- Relationship with the curriculum: 20 marks.\\n- Mode of presentation and write up: 25 marks.\\n- Beauty and perfection: 15 marks.\\n- Exhibition: 10 marks.\\n- The total is 100 marks."},{"Title":"Still Model","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.7 D (Model section) 4, p.71 and E 4, p.75","Sections":{"About":["A three dimensional model made with different geometric shapes to show a maths idea.","This item is held for LP, UP, HS and HSS/VHSS."],"TimeAndFormat":["This is an on-the-spot competition of 3 hours."],"Rules":["The model must fit in a space of 2 square metres.","Materials that are friendly to nature (eco friendly) are used."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Knowledge of content and mathematical value: 30 marks.","Relationship with the curriculum: 20 marks.","Mode of presentation and write up: 25 marks.","Utility and craftsmanship: 15 marks.","Exhibition: 10 marks.","The total is 100 marks."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A three dimensional model made with different geometric shapes to show a maths idea.\\n- This item is held for LP, UP, HS and HSS/VHSS.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- This is an on-the-spot competition of 3 hours.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The model must fit in a space of 2 square metres.\\n- Materials that are friendly to nature (eco friendly) are used.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Knowledge of content and mathematical value: 30 marks.\\n- Relationship with the curriculum: 20 marks.\\n- Mode of presentation and write up: 25 marks.\\n- Utility and craftsmanship: 15 marks.\\n- Exhibition: 10 marks.\\n- The total is 100 marks."},{"Title":"Working Model","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.7 D (Model section) 5, p.71 and E 5, p.75","Sections":{"About":["A model that can show, explain or make clear maths ideas by working. This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS."],"TimeAndFormat":["This is an on-the-spot competition of 3 hours."],"Rules":["The model must fit in a space of 2 square metres.","The Green Protocol must be followed strictly. Materials that are friendly to nature are used."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Knowledge of content and mathematical value: 30 marks.","Relationship with the curriculum: 20 marks.","Mode of presentation and write up: 25 marks.","Utility and craftsmanship: 15 marks.","Exhibition: 10 marks.","The total is 100 marks."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A model that can show, explain or make clear maths ideas by working. This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- This is an on-the-spot competition of 3 hours.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The model must fit in a space of 2 square metres.\\n- The Green Protocol must be followed strictly. Materials that are friendly to nature are used.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Knowledge of content and mathematical value: 30 marks.\\n- Relationship with the curriculum: 20 marks.\\n- Mode of presentation and write up: 25 marks.\\n- Utility and craftsmanship: 15 marks.\\n- Exhibition: 10 marks.\\n- The total is 100 marks."},{"Title":"Pure Construction","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.7 D 6, pp.71-72 and E 6, p.76","Sections":{"About":["This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS. The constructions are made on a chart."],"TimeAndFormat":["This is an on-the-spot competition of 3 hours."],"Rules":["Only a ruler (without markings, with no scale) and a compass can be used.","In the making, weight is given to the basic parts of the construction: fineness and accuracy.","Draw with a pencil. Colour is not allowed. Up to 3 charts can be used.","The size of the construction is the size of the chart."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Knowledge of content and mathematical value: 30 marks.","Relationship with the curriculum: 20 marks.","Mode of presentation and write up: 25 marks.","Accuracy, preciseness and beauty: 15 marks.","Exhibition: 10 marks.","The total is 100 marks."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS. The constructions are made on a chart.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- This is an on-the-spot competition of 3 hours.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only a ruler (without markings, with no scale) and a compass can be used.\\n- In the making, weight is given to the basic parts of the construction: fineness and accuracy.\\n- Draw with a pencil. Colour is not allowed. Up to 3 charts can be used.\\n- The size of the construction is the size of the chart.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Knowledge of content and mathematical value: 30 marks.\\n- Relationship with the curriculum: 20 marks.\\n- Mode of presentation and write up: 25 marks.\\n- Accuracy, preciseness and beauty: 15 marks.\\n- Exhibition: 10 marks.\\n- The total is 100 marks."},{"Title":"Construction Using Geogebra Software","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.7 D 7, p.72 and E 7, p.76","Sections":{"About":["GeoGebra is software that helps the study of mathematics. It is used in class rooms to show abstract and concrete ideas of geometry in an attractive and moving form. This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS.","The competition is on the spot."],"TimeAndFormat":["As part of the competition the competitor makes one applet with GeoGebra in 1 and a half hours. It must be saved in the fixed time.","The presentation takes at most 5 minutes."],"Rules":["The organisers give the laptops.","Depending on how many laptops there are, the competitors are made into batches. If more than one batch is needed, the applets saved by the first batch are moved to a pen drive and copied to the laptop given to the judges, with the code number of the competitor as the file name.","The presentation starts, by code number, after the files of all competitors are saved.","A projector and a screen can be used for the presentation.","The presentation is recorded on video, and this can be used by the judges for evaluation."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Ideas of the textbook, growth and continuity of the ideas: 20 marks.","Attractiveness, dynamism and composition: 20 marks.","Technical excellence and effective use of tools: 40 marks.","Excellence in the presentation and the ability to exchange ideas: 20 marks.","The total is 100 marks."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- GeoGebra is software that helps the study of mathematics. It is used in class rooms to show abstract and concrete ideas of geometry in an attractive and moving form. This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS.\\n- The competition is on the spot.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- As part of the competition the competitor makes one applet with GeoGebra in 1 and a half hours. It must be saved in the fixed time.\\n- The presentation takes at most 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The organisers give the laptops.\\n- Depending on how many laptops there are, the competitors are made into batches. If more than one batch is needed, the applets saved by the first batch are moved to a pen drive and copied to the laptop given to the judges, with the code number of the competitor as the file name.\\n- The presentation starts, by code number, after the files of all competitors are saved.\\n- A projector and a screen can be used for the presentation.\\n- The presentation is recorded on video, and this can be used by the judges for evaluation.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Ideas of the textbook, growth and continuity of the ideas: 20 marks.\\n- Attractiveness, dynamism and composition: 20 marks.\\n- Technical excellence and effective use of tools: 40 marks.\\n- Excellence in the presentation and the ability to exchange ideas: 20 marks.\\n- The total is 100 marks."},{"Title":"Puzzle","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.7 D 11, p.74 and E 9, p.76","Sections":{"About":["Questions that arouse curiosity and hold ideas of mathematics. This item is held for LP, UP, HS and HSS/VHSS."],"TimeAndFormat":["This is an on-the-spot competition of 3 hours."],"Rules":["Only one puzzle can be presented."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Knowledge of content and mathematical value: 30 marks.","Relationship with the curriculum: 20 marks.","Mode of presentation and write up: 25 marks.","Logical thinking and reasoning: 15 marks.","Exhibition: 10 marks.","The total is 100 marks."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Questions that arouse curiosity and hold ideas of mathematics. This item is held for LP, UP, HS and HSS/VHSS.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- This is an on-the-spot competition of 3 hours.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one puzzle can be presented.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Knowledge of content and mathematical value: 30 marks.\\n- Relationship with the curriculum: 20 marks.\\n- Mode of presentation and write up: 25 marks.\\n- Logical thinking and reasoning: 15 marks.\\n- Exhibition: 10 marks.\\n- The total is 100 marks."},{"Title":"Game","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.7 D 10, p.74 and E 8, p.76","Sections":{"About":["A game that two or more persons can play at the same time and that holds values of mathematics. This item is held for UP, HS and HSS/VHSS."],"TimeAndFormat":["This is an on-the-spot competition of 3 hours."],"Rules":["Players and pieces (tokens) are a must.","The game must have a rule.","The final result of the game must be decided.","Only one game can be presented in this item."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Knowledge of content and mathematical value: 30 marks.","Relationship with the curriculum: 20 marks.","Mode of presentation and write up: 25 marks.","Enjoyment value and creativity of the game: 15 marks.","Exhibition: 10 marks.","The total is 100 marks."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A game that two or more persons can play at the same time and that holds values of mathematics. This item is held for UP, HS and HSS/VHSS.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- This is an on-the-spot competition of 3 hours.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Players and pieces (tokens) are a must.\\n- The game must have a rule.\\n- The final result of the game must be decided.\\n- Only one game can be presented in this item.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Knowledge of content and mathematical value: 30 marks.\\n- Relationship with the curriculum: 20 marks.\\n- Mode of presentation and write up: 25 marks.\\n- Enjoyment value and creativity of the game: 15 marks.\\n- Exhibition: 10 marks.\\n- The total is 100 marks."},{"Title":"Single Project","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.7 D 8, pp.72-73 and E 10, pp.76-77","Sections":{"About":["A project is a study based on research. A project report is a must, with at most 50 pages. This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS."],"TimeAndFormat":["The project is presented in at most 10 minutes. Only 5 charts, models or slides can be used to help the presentation."],"Rules":["The subject must be about mathematics. A study done with statistics on a social subject is not a maths project.","The project report is a hand written copy. It is written on one side of A4 paper and bound.","The subject is written on the first page, outside the cover. A collection is on page 2, and the references are shown at the end.","Three photocopies of the project report are given (binding is not needed).","ICT tools can also be used.","This is not an on-the-spot competition."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Knowledge of content and mathematical value: 30 marks.","Relationship with the curriculum: 20 marks.","Mode of presentation: 25 marks.","Project report and supporting materials: 15 marks.","Exhibition: 10 marks.","The total is 100 marks."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A project is a study based on research. A project report is a must, with at most 50 pages. This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The project is presented in at most 10 minutes. Only 5 charts, models or slides can be used to help the presentation.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The subject must be about mathematics. A study done with statistics on a social subject is not a maths project.\\n- The project report is a hand written copy. It is written on one side of A4 paper and bound.\\n- The subject is written on the first page, outside the cover. A collection is on page 2, and the references are shown at the end.\\n- Three photocopies of the project report are given (binding is not needed).\\n- ICT tools can also be used.\\n- This is not an on-the-spot competition.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Knowledge of content and mathematical value: 30 marks.\\n- Relationship with the curriculum: 20 marks.\\n- Mode of presentation: 25 marks.\\n- Project report and supporting materials: 15 marks.\\n- Exhibition: 10 marks.\\n- The total is 100 marks."},{"Title":"Group Project","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.7 D 9, p.74 and E 11, p.77","Sections":{"About":["All the rules of the Single Project also bind this item. Two children take part. The part of each child must be clear. This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS."],"TimeAndFormat":["The project is presented in at most 10 minutes. Only 5 charts, models or slides can be used to help the presentation."],"Rules":["Three photocopies of the project report are given (binding is not needed).","This is not an on-the-spot competition."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Knowledge of content and mathematical value: 30 marks.","Relationship with the curriculum: 20 marks.","Mode of presentation: 25 marks.","Project report and supporting materials: 15 marks.","Exhibition: 10 marks.","The total is 100 marks."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- All the rules of the Single Project also bind this item. Two children take part. The part of each child must be clear. This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The project is presented in at most 10 minutes. Only 5 charts, models or slides can be used to help the presentation.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Three photocopies of the project report are given (binding is not needed).\\n- This is not an on-the-spot competition.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Knowledge of content and mathematical value: 30 marks.\\n- Relationship with the curriculum: 20 marks.\\n- Mode of presentation: 25 marks.\\n- Project report and supporting materials: 15 marks.\\n- Exhibition: 10 marks.\\n- The total is 100 marks."},{"Title":"Maths Magazine","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.7 A, p.67 and G, pp.79-80 and E 13, p.77","Sections":{"About":["The Magazine competition is held for LP up to the sub-district level, for UP up to the revenue district level, and for HS and HSS/VHSS up to the state level. It is held along with the maths fair.","The maths club members of the school prepare the magazine. The children do not take part in it."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["The magazine is given to the committee on the registration day of the Mathematics Fair.","The result of the magazine is not counted for the championship of the fair.","The content can hold maths stories, poems, songs, riddles, puzzles, games, number patterns, geometric patterns, odd calculations, maths pictures, maths cartoons, history of maths, scientists, events, maths proverbs, old sayings, the link between maths and nature, and other things about mathematics.","Pictures or notes cut and stuck from other sources are not allowed.","The magazine is a hand written copy, with a back cover, and is bound. Spiral binding is not allowed.","The magazine has one name. The name of the school, the sub-district, the education district or the revenue district, and other identifying marks must not be in it. Marks that help identify the magazine are not counted in the evaluation if found.","Write on one side of an A4 paper only. The magazine can have at most 50 pages, including the back cover.","After the evaluation, the magazines other than the one that qualifies for the next level are punched and given back at the venue of the fair."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Mathematical value: 40 marks.","Variety: 30 marks.","Layout: 20 marks.","Accuracy and beauty: 10 marks.","The total is 100 marks."],"Points":null,"Notes":["The list of marks on p.80 names the third and fourth items as arrangement of the content (20) and binding and layout of the magazine (10). The score table on p.77 names them Layout (20) and Accuracy and beauty (10)."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The Magazine competition is held for LP up to the sub-district level, for UP up to the revenue district level, and for HS and HSS/VHSS up to the state level. It is held along with the maths fair.\\n- The maths club members of the school prepare the magazine. The children do not take part in it.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The magazine is given to the committee on the registration day of the Mathematics Fair.\\n- The result of the magazine is not counted for the championship of the fair.\\n- The content can hold maths stories, poems, songs, riddles, puzzles, games, number patterns, geometric patterns, odd calculations, maths pictures, maths cartoons, history of maths, scientists, events, maths proverbs, old sayings, the link between maths and nature, and other things about mathematics.\\n- Pictures or notes cut and stuck from other sources are not allowed.\\n- The magazine is a hand written copy, with a back cover, and is bound. Spiral binding is not allowed.\\n- The magazine has one name. The name of the school, the sub-district, the education district or the revenue district, and other identifying marks must not be in it. Marks that help identify the magazine are not counted in the evaluation if found.\\n- Write on one side of an A4 paper only. The magazine can have at most 50 pages, including the back cover.\\n- After the evaluation, the magazines other than the one that qualifies for the next level are punched and given back at the venue of the fair.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Mathematical value: 40 marks.\\n- Variety: 30 marks.\\n- Layout: 20 marks.\\n- Accuracy and beauty: 10 marks.\\n- The total is 100 marks.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The list of marks on p.80 names the third and fourth items as arrangement of the content (20) and binding and layout of the magazine (10). The score table on p.77 names them Layout (20) and Accuracy and beauty (10)."},{"Title":"Maths Quiz","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.7 F, pp.77-79","Sections":{"About":["The maths quiz is a useful way to find maths talent. The grade is decided from the points of the first place winner in the quiz."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["School level (LP, UP, HS, HSS/VHSS): the head master or principal, with the maths club coordinator, is responsible. First, second and third place winners get certificates and encouragement awards. The child who qualifies for first place in each section goes to the sub-district quiz, with a certificate from the head master or principal.","Sub-district level: the sub-district education officer fixes the dates and places. First, second and third place winners get certificates and encouragement awards. The children who qualify for first and second place in each section go to the revenue district quiz.","Revenue district level (HS and HSS/VHSS): the quiz is held under the Deputy Director of Education. The first and second place winners in each section get certificates and encouragement awards, and go to the state quiz.","State level (HS and HSS/VHSS): only the first and second place winners of the revenue district quiz can take part. Competitors get participant certificates with the grade. The first, second and third place winners get a certificate and a cash award."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The maths quiz is a useful way to find maths talent. The grade is decided from the points of the first place winner in the quiz.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- School level (LP, UP, HS, HSS/VHSS): the head master or principal, with the maths club coordinator, is responsible. First, second and third place winners get certificates and encouragement awards. The child who qualifies for first place in each section goes to the sub-district quiz, with a certificate from the head master or principal.\\n- Sub-district level: the sub-district education officer fixes the dates and places. First, second and third place winners get certificates and encouragement awards. The children who qualify for first and second place in each section go to the revenue district quiz.\\n- Revenue district level (HS and HSS/VHSS): the quiz is held under the Deputy Director of Education. The first and second place winners in each section get certificates and encouragement awards, and go to the state quiz.\\n- State level (HS and HSS/VHSS): only the first and second place winners of the revenue district quiz can take part. Competitors get participant certificates with the grade. The first, second and third place winners get a certificate and a cash award."},{"Title":"Madhava Paper Presentation","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.7 G (new item), pp.80-81","Sections":{"About":["This is a new item for the UP section only. It is held up to the sub-district level.","The winner of first place at the school level can take part in the sub-district competition. The first, second and third place winners at the sub-district competition get certificates and encouragement awards.","At the sub-district level, three subjects are given beforehand, and the judges draw one by lot. The competitor gets 2 hours to prepare the paper."],"TimeAndFormat":["The presentation takes 5 minutes and the interview 3 minutes at every level."],"Rules":["The subject of the paper presentation is decided at the state level each year.","A stamped A4 paper is given to prepare the paper.","The paper for the presentation is hand written, with at most 5 pages.","The competitor can read from the paper.","A mobile phone is not allowed for any reason."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Presentation: 30 marks.","Content and mathematical value: 30 marks.","Interview: 20 marks.","Paper and supporting materials: 20 marks.","The total is 100 marks."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This is a new item for the UP section only. It is held up to the sub-district level.\\n- The winner of first place at the school level can take part in the sub-district competition. The first, second and third place winners at the sub-district competition get certificates and encouragement awards.\\n- At the sub-district level, three subjects are given beforehand, and the judges draw one by lot. The competitor gets 2 hours to prepare the paper.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The presentation takes 5 minutes and the interview 3 minutes at every level.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The subject of the paper presentation is decided at the state level each year.\\n- A stamped A4 paper is given to prepare the paper.\\n- The paper for the presentation is hand written, with at most 5 pages.\\n- The competitor can read from the paper.\\n- A mobile phone is not allowed for any reason.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Presentation: 30 marks.\\n- Content and mathematical value: 30 marks.\\n- Interview: 20 marks.\\n- Paper and supporting materials: 20 marks.\\n- The total is 100 marks."},{"Title":"Bhaskaracharya Seminar","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.7 H, pp.81-84","Sections":{"About":["This competition is for the HS section only. It is held at school, sub-district, revenue district and state levels. The subject is decided at the state level each year."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["The first place winner at the school level can take part at the sub-district level. The school level competition is the responsibility of the head master under the maths club coordinator.","The sub-district competition is held under the sub-district education officer. The first and second place winners can take part at the revenue district level, which is held under the Deputy Director of Education. The first and second place winners at the revenue district can take part at the state level.","In each section the first, second and third place winners get certificates, encouragement awards and a cash award. Competitors at the state level get a participant certificate with the grade.","The subject of the paper presentation is decided at the state level each year.","At the sub-district and revenue district levels, three subjects are given beforehand, and the judges draw one of them by lot. The competitor gets 2 hours to prepare the paper.","At the state level the subject is not given beforehand. On the morning of the competition the subject is given, and the competitor gets 3 hours to prepare the paper, a chart and a multimedia presentation.","The competitors bring a laptop or charts. The internet is provided at the revenue district and state levels. A printed A4 paper to prepare the paper is given.","The paper for the presentation must be hand written, with at most 5 pages. The competitor can read from the paper.","The presentation takes 5 minutes and the interview 3 minutes, at every level.","A mobile phone, Chat GPT, Artificial Intelligence and websites that work with their help are not allowed for any reason."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Presentation: 30 marks.","Content and mathematical value: 30 marks.","Interview: 20 marks.","Paper and supporting materials: 20 marks.","The total is 100 marks."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This competition is for the HS section only. It is held at school, sub-district, revenue district and state levels. The subject is decided at the state level each year.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The first place winner at the school level can take part at the sub-district level. The school level competition is the responsibility of the head master under the maths club coordinator.\\n- The sub-district competition is held under the sub-district education officer. The first and second place winners can take part at the revenue district level, which is held under the Deputy Director of Education. The first and second place winners at the revenue district can take part at the state level.\\n- In each section the first, second and third place winners get certificates, encouragement awards and a cash award. Competitors at the state level get a participant certificate with the grade.\\n- The subject of the paper presentation is decided at the state level each year.\\n- At the sub-district and revenue district levels, three subjects are given beforehand, and the judges draw one of them by lot. The competitor gets 2 hours to prepare the paper.\\n- At the state level the subject is not given beforehand. On the morning of the competition the subject is given, and the competitor gets 3 hours to prepare the paper, a chart and a multimedia presentation.\\n- The competitors bring a laptop or charts. The internet is provided at the revenue district and state levels. A printed A4 paper to prepare the paper is given.\\n- The paper for the presentation must be hand written, with at most 5 pages. The competitor can read from the paper.\\n- The presentation takes 5 minutes and the interview 3 minutes, at every level.\\n- A mobile phone, Chat GPT, Artificial Intelligence and websites that work with their help are not allowed for any reason.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Presentation: 30 marks.\\n- Content and mathematical value: 30 marks.\\n- Interview: 20 marks.\\n- Paper and supporting materials: 20 marks.\\n- The total is 100 marks."},{"Title":"Ramanujan Paper Presentation","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.7 I, pp.84-86","Sections":{"About":["This competition is for the HSS/VHSS section only. It is held at school, sub-district, revenue district and state levels. The subject is decided at the state level each year."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["The first place winner at the school level can take part at the sub-district level. The school level competition is the responsibility of the head master or principal under the maths club coordinator.","The sub-district competition is held under the sub-district education officer. The first and second place winners can take part at the revenue district level, which is held under the Deputy Director of Education. The first and second place winners at the revenue district can take part at the state level.","In each section the first and second place winners get certificates, encouragement awards and a cash award. Competitors at the state level get a participant certificate with the grade. The first three places at the state level get a cash award and an encouragement award.","The subject of the paper presentation is decided at the state level each year.","At the sub-district and revenue district levels, three subjects are given beforehand, and the judges draw one of them by lot. The competitor gets 2 hours to prepare the paper.","At the state level the subject is not given beforehand. On the morning of the competition the subject is given, and the competitor gets 3 hours to prepare the paper, a chart and a multimedia presentation.","The competitors bring a laptop or charts. The internet is provided at the revenue district and state levels. A printed A4 paper to prepare the paper is given.","The paper for the presentation must be hand written, with at most 5 pages. The competitor can read from the paper.","The presentation takes 5 minutes and the interview 3 minutes, at every level.","A mobile phone, Chat GPT, Artificial Intelligence and websites that work with their help are not allowed for any reason."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Presentation: 30 marks.","Content and mathematical value: 30 marks.","Interview: 20 marks.","Paper and supporting materials: 20 marks.","The total is 100 marks."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This competition is for the HSS/VHSS section only. It is held at school, sub-district, revenue district and state levels. The subject is decided at the state level each year.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The first place winner at the school level can take part at the sub-district level. The school level competition is the responsibility of the head master or principal under the maths club coordinator.\\n- The sub-district competition is held under the sub-district education officer. The first and second place winners can take part at the revenue district level, which is held under the Deputy Director of Education. The first and second place winners at the revenue district can take part at the state level.\\n- In each section the first and second place winners get certificates, encouragement awards and a cash award. Competitors at the state level get a participant certificate with the grade. The first three places at the state level get a cash award and an encouragement award.\\n- The subject of the paper presentation is decided at the state level each year.\\n- At the sub-district and revenue district levels, three subjects are given beforehand, and the judges draw one of them by lot. The competitor gets 2 hours to prepare the paper.\\n- At the state level the subject is not given beforehand. On the morning of the competition the subject is given, and the competitor gets 3 hours to prepare the paper, a chart and a multimedia presentation.\\n- The competitors bring a laptop or charts. The internet is provided at the revenue district and state levels. A printed A4 paper to prepare the paper is given.\\n- The paper for the presentation must be hand written, with at most 5 pages. The competitor can read from the paper.\\n- The presentation takes 5 minutes and the interview 3 minutes, at every level.\\n- A mobile phone, Chat GPT, Artificial Intelligence and websites that work with their help are not allowed for any reason.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Presentation: 30 marks.\\n- Content and mathematical value: 30 marks.\\n- Interview: 20 marks.\\n- Paper and supporting materials: 20 marks.\\n- The total is 100 marks."},{"Title":"Talent Search Examination","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.7 J, pp.87-92","Sections":{"About":["This competition is for the UP, HS and HSS/VHSS sections. It is held at school, sub-district, revenue district and state levels."],"TimeAndFormat":["School level: 14 questions (6 of 1 mark, 5 of 2 marks, 3 of 3 marks), 25 marks, 1 hour.","Sub-district level, UP and HS: 23 questions (5 of 1 mark, 9 of 2 marks, 9 of 3 marks), 50 marks, 2 hours.","Sub-district level, HSS and VHSE: 20 questions (10 of 2 marks and 10 of 3 marks), 50 marks, 2 hours.","Revenue district level, HS: 5 questions of 1 mark, 10 of 2 marks and 5 of 5 marks, 50 marks, 2 hours.","Revenue district level, HSS/VHSS: the paper has 8 questions of 5 marks and 3 questions of 10 marks. The competitor writes 6 of the 5 mark questions and 2 of the 10 mark questions, 50 marks, 2 hours.","State level (1 day), HS, part 1: 5 questions of 1 mark, 10 of 2 marks and 5 of 5 marks (20 questions), 50 marks, 2 hours.","State level, HSS/VHSS, part 1: the competitor writes 5 of 8 questions of 10 marks, 50 marks, 2 hours.","State level, part 2 (both sections): a class of about 1 hour from a resource person that helps grow interest in maths. Then each child writes a note on the subject of the class, of at most 2 pages, in 45 minutes. Then an interview is held on the note, 3 to 5 minutes for each child. Part 2 carries 10 marks."],"Rules":["A winner of first place at the school level can take part at the sub-district level. The head master or principal, with the maths club coordinator, is responsible for the school exam.","The school level question paper is made by the head master or principal with the help of the school maths club, as per the guidelines. The head master or principal checks the papers and declares the result.","The sub-district exam is held under the sub-district education officer. The first and second place winners can take part at the revenue district level, which is held under the Deputy Director of Education. The first and second place winners of the revenue district (HS and HSS/VHSS) can take part at the state level.","The question paper of the sub-district exam is made by the Deputy Director of Education with the maths club association, and the exam is held on the same day in all sub-districts of the district. The sub-district education officer holds it with the help of the sub-district maths club association, checks the papers and declares the result.","The question paper of the revenue district exam is made at the state level. It is held on the day fixed by the Director of General Education, by the Deputy Directors of Education with the help of the revenue district maths club association. They check the papers and declare the result.","In the afternoon of the revenue district exam, a class is given to both sections that introduces different areas of mathematics and the chances for further study.","The state level exam is held under the Director of General Education in two parts."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This competition is for the UP, HS and HSS/VHSS sections. It is held at school, sub-district, revenue district and state levels.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- School level: 14 questions (6 of 1 mark, 5 of 2 marks, 3 of 3 marks), 25 marks, 1 hour.\\n- Sub-district level, UP and HS: 23 questions (5 of 1 mark, 9 of 2 marks, 9 of 3 marks), 50 marks, 2 hours.\\n- Sub-district level, HSS and VHSE: 20 questions (10 of 2 marks and 10 of 3 marks), 50 marks, 2 hours.\\n- Revenue district level, HS: 5 questions of 1 mark, 10 of 2 marks and 5 of 5 marks, 50 marks, 2 hours.\\n- Revenue district level, HSS/VHSS: the paper has 8 questions of 5 marks and 3 questions of 10 marks. The competitor writes 6 of the 5 mark questions and 2 of the 10 mark questions, 50 marks, 2 hours.\\n- State level (1 day), HS, part 1: 5 questions of 1 mark, 10 of 2 marks and 5 of 5 marks (20 questions), 50 marks, 2 hours.\\n- State level, HSS/VHSS, part 1: the competitor writes 5 of 8 questions of 10 marks, 50 marks, 2 hours.\\n- State level, part 2 (both sections): a class of about 1 hour from a resource person that helps grow interest in maths. Then each child writes a note on the subject of the class, of at most 2 pages, in 45 minutes. Then an interview is held on the note, 3 to 5 minutes for each child. Part 2 carries 10 marks.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A winner of first place at the school level can take part at the sub-district level. The head master or principal, with the maths club coordinator, is responsible for the school exam.\\n- The school level question paper is made by the head master or principal with the help of the school maths club, as per the guidelines. The head master or principal checks the papers and declares the result.\\n- The sub-district exam is held under the sub-district education officer. The first and second place winners can take part at the revenue district level, which is held under the Deputy Director of Education. The first and second place winners of the revenue district (HS and HSS/VHSS) can take part at the state level.\\n- The question paper of the sub-district exam is made by the Deputy Director of Education with the maths club association, and the exam is held on the same day in all sub-districts of the district. The sub-district education officer holds it with the help of the sub-district maths club association, checks the papers and declares the result.\\n- The question paper of the revenue district exam is made at the state level. It is held on the day fixed by the Director of General Education, by the Deputy Directors of Education with the help of the revenue district maths club association. They check the papers and declare the result.\\n- In the afternoon of the revenue district exam, a class is given to both sections that introduces different areas of mathematics and the chances for further study.\\n- The state level exam is held under the Director of General Education in two parts."}]'),s=[],r=[{Key:"SubDistrictRegistrationFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Registration fee at the sub-district fair",Value:"Rs. 20 per child, collected only from children of classes 9, 10, 11 and 12",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.2 B 7(b), p.12"},{Key:"AppealFeeSubDistrict",Kind:"fee",Label:"Appeal fee, sub-district level",Value:"Rs. 1000 per appeal",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.4 A, p.30 and C, p.32"},{Key:"AppealFeeRevenueDistrict",Kind:"fee",Label:"Appeal fee, revenue district level",Value:"Rs. 1500 per appeal",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.4 A, p.30 and D, p.32"},{Key:"AppealFeeState",Kind:"fee",Label:"Appeal fee, state level",Value:"Rs. 2000 per appeal",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.4 A, p.30 and E, p.33"},{Key:"AppealFeeHigher",Kind:"fee",Label:"Appeal fee, higher appeal",Value:"Rs. 2500 per appeal",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.4 A, p.30"},{Key:"CertificateReplacementFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Fee for a new certificate when one is lost or has errors",Value:"Rs. 250 by demand draft in the name of the Director of General Education",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.1 A 16, p.6"},{Key:"Announcements",Kind:"news",Label:"Order printed with the manual",Value:[{Date:"2025-09-12",Title:"Sasthrolsavam to be held from school level this year",Text:"By order No. DGE/7858/2024 dated 12 September 2025 the Additional Director (Academic) of the Directorate of General Education issued the revised Sasthrolsavam Manual 2025 and gave the direction to hold the Sasthrolsavam from school level this year. The order refers to Government orders (Rt) No. 146/2025/GEDN dated 23 August 2025, No. 118/2024/GEDN dated 20 September 2024 and No. 116/2024/GEDN dated 19 September 2024.",Url:"https://mela.kite.kerala.gov.in/2026/entry_forms/sasthrolsavam_manual_2025.pdf"}],Source:"Manual 2025 order page, PDF p.1"}],h=[{Claim:"Rules for every fair (categories, levels, eligibility, online entry, grades, appeals, championship, committees, judges) and the Mathematics Fair chapter (items, rules, score indicators, quiz, magazine, paper presentations, talent search) are taken from the manual. The entry forms and annexures at the end of the manual were read for the entry steps.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Kerala School Sasthrolsavam Manual 2025, General Education Department, Government of Kerala, Chapters 1-5, Chapter 7 and the annexures",Url:"https://mela.kite.kerala.gov.in/2026/entry_forms/sasthrolsavam_manual_2025.pdf"},{Claim:"The list of items per group (LP, UP, HS, HSS/VHSS) and the item type (team or individual) is the official 2026 item list.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Kerala School Sasthrolsavam Item List 2026, KITE (Kerala Infrastructure and Technology for Education)",Url:"https://mela.kite.kerala.gov.in/2026/index.php/Home/item_list"}],l={TemplateKey:e,Year:2025,Note:t,Page:a,ParticipantTypes:i,AgeGroups:n,Competitions:o,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:r,Evidence:h};export{n as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,o as Competitions,h as Evidence,t as Note,a as Page,i as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,r as Variables,c as Year,l as default};
